---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const toc = [
  { id: 'policy', label: 'always-bump-minor' },
  { id: 'steps', label: 'Upgrade steps' },
  { id: 'map', label: 'What breaks' },
  { id: 'paths', label: '6.0 absolute paths' },
  { id: 'hopper', label: '6.1 Hopper' },
  { id: 'evidence', label: '6.2 Evidence' },
  { id: 'captures', label: '6.3 capture accounting' },
  { id: 'sockets', label: '6.4 WebSocket field' },
  { id: 'nulls', label: '6.5 nulls & contracts' },
  { id: 'kuna', label: '6.6 Evidence & ADB' },
  { id: 'six-seven', label: '6.7 no own breaks' },
  { id: 'formats', label: '6.8 Node & schemas' },
  { id: 'desktop', label: '6.9 contracts' },
  { id: 'related', label: 'Related' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="REA upgrade runbook: breaking changes 6.0–6.9.0 | rea.run"
  description="Operator runbook for rea-agents 6.0 through 6.9.0: absolute MCP paths, Evidence shape, the 6.8 Node floor, compact MCP schemas by default, and the 6.9 field contracts. 6.7 has no breaking section of its own."
  path="/docs/breaking/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-toc hidden md:block">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-3">On this page</p>
        {toc.map((item) => <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>)}
      </aside>
      <article class="prose-page">
        <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/changelog/">← Changelog</a></p>
        <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">Docs · pin 6.9.0</p>
        <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">Upgrade without breaking your runbooks</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">
          From <strong>6.0.0</strong> (2026-10-08) through <strong>6.9.0</strong> (2026-11-12), several minor releases changed MCP inputs, Evidence shape, Node engines, and saved captures.
          This page is the operator checklist for those breaks. Dates are GitHub release <code>published_at</code> values. The teaching pin on rea.run is <code>rea-agents@6.9.0</code>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="policy">always-bump-minor is not a compatibility promise</h2>
        <p>
          Upstream’s 6.2 migration guide states the policy in one sentence: the repository uses <code>always-bump-minor</code>, <strong>including breaking releases</strong>. A minor number does not mean old scripts, old Evidence files, or old captures still validate.
          npm <code>latest</code> checked on <strong>2026-11-13 17:02:45 CST (Asia/Shanghai)</strong> was <code>6.9.0</code>. Floating <code>@latest</code> in a runbook will pick up the next minor whenever it publishes, breaks included.
        </p>
        <p>
          The 6.9.0 client matrix is on the <a href="/docs/clients/">client page</a> (28 <code>--client</code> ids). Confirm with doctor before treating a registration as aligned. 6.6.0 is a GitHub tag that npm does not publish; installing npm 6.7.0 is how those 6.6 breaks arrive.
        </p>

        <h2 id="steps">Upgrade steps</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Record the pin you run today: the version in MCP <code>args</code>, and <code>npm view rea-agents version</code> if you use a global CLI. They can differ.</li>
          <li>Read every row you will cross in the table below. Jumping 6.1 → 6.9.0 still includes the 6.2 through 6.8 contracts. Move Node to <code>^22.23.4 || ^24.22.1 || &gt;=26.12.1</code> before you install 6.8.0 or 6.9.0. The 6.8.0 note says the installer does not upgrade Node, and that Node 23 and 25 are unsupported.</li>
          <li>Copy Evidence bundles, analysis snapshots, and process captures to a side directory. Do not rewrite them in place.</li>
          <li>
            Point the client at the pin and approve a scoped setup plan:
            <pre><code>{`npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 setup --client codex --dry-run --json
# review, then:
npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 setup --client codex --yes --json`}</code></pre>
          </li>
          <li>Restart or reconnect the agent. Cached <code>tools/list</code> schemas from the previous package are a common first failure.</li>
          <li>Run <code>npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 doctor --json</code> and attach the JSON to the change ticket. Record <code>node -v</code> next to it.</li>
          <li>Re-run one authorized target you already understand. Diff field names before you trust a dashboard or a script.</li>
          <li>If a consumer still reads <code>structuredContent.result</code>, switch it to <code>normalized_result</code> (6.2). If it reads <code>network.websocket_events</code>, switch it to <code>network.websocket_connections</code> (6.4). There is no legacy alias for the WebSocket field.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Manual MCP JSON for this pin:</p>
        <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rea": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "rea-agents@6.9.0", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

        <h2 id="map">Operator-relevant breaks, 6.0 through 6.9.0</h2>
        <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Version</th><th>Published (UTC)</th><th>What your scripts notice</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>6.0.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-08 09:40</td>
                <td>MCP filesystem inputs must be absolute host paths. CLI relative paths still work.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.1.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-09 01:08</td>
                <td>Hopper regex is ECMAScript Unicode, with a five-second worker deadline. <code>set_current_document</code> is gone.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.2.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-09 16:51</td>
                <td>Success Evidence is the structured payload. Read <code>normalized_result</code>. Old wrappers, snapshots, and v3 captures do not migrate by field-stuffing.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.3.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-09 23:56</td>
                <td>Captures need current producer accounting and transaction identity. Do not synthesize missing web-diff dimensions.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.4.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-11 03:58</td>
                <td><code>network.websocket_connections</code> replaces <code>network.websocket_events</code>. Several stored graph schemas also change.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.5.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-14 12:32</td>
                <td><code>attached</code> / source name / segment length / <code>command_path</code> may be null; <code>--filter-output</code> emits JSON null; call-graph <code>{"{"} graph, limitations {"}"}</code>; <code>binary_session</code> drops repeated tools catalog; ADB <code>replace_requested</code> / nullable <code>replaced</code>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.6.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-18 03:40</td>
                <td>GitHub only (not npm). Saved Evidence must be regenerated. ADB <code>version_code</code> is a decimal string. <a href="#kuna">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.7.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-18 07:45</td>
                <td>No <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code> heading of its own. npm 6.7.0 is the first published package that includes the 6.6 breaks. <a href="#six-seven">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.8.0</td>
                <td>2026-10-25 08:36</td>
                <td>Node floor moves. MCP input ads default to compact. <code>analyze_function</code> defaults to a summary. JSON Lines gains a metadata record. <a href="#formats">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>6.9.0</td>
                <td>2026-11-12 08:59</td>
                <td>Settings use <code>update_mode</code>. <code>rea mcp add --command</code> is local stdio only. Many Evidence readers must accept nulls, new unions, and the 1,024-element MCP input default. <a href="#desktop">Steps</a>.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Earlier majors in the same ten days (4.0.0, 5.0.0) have their own breaks. They are listed on the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>. This runbook starts where MCP path and Evidence consumers usually break: 6.0.</p>

        <h2 id="paths">6.0.0 — absolute MCP paths</h2>
        <p>
          Published 2026-10-08. MCP filesystem inputs require absolute host paths. That includes target and snapshot paths, Evidence bundle paths, managed and firmware inputs, browser and Electron launch paths, and expected server paths.
          Optional paths stay optional. A call shaped like <code>open_binary</code> with <code>"./app"</code> must send <code>/home/analyst/app</code> or <code>C:\analysis\app</code>.
          The CLI still accepts operator-relative paths. Agents that build MCP arguments from a relative workspace root need <code>pwd</code> joined in, not a string the model invented.
        </p>
        <p>Sources: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/948" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#948</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1004" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1004</a>, release <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.0.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.0.0</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="hopper">6.1.0 — Hopper callers</h2>
        <p>
          Published 2026-10-09. If you drive Hopper search from REA: regex mode is ECMAScript Unicode syntax, not Python <code>re</code>. Matching runs in a cancellable worker with a five-second deadline. Literal mode keeps Unicode casefold matching.
          <code>set_current_document</code> is removed. Switch targets with <code>open_binary</code>. Document arguments are scoped to the active target.
        </p>

        <h2 id="evidence">6.2.0 — Evidence, snapshots, and saved inventories</h2>
        <p>
          Published 2026-10-09. Read <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/rea-agents-6.5.0/docs/migration-6.2.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">docs/migration-6.2.md</a> on the 6.5.0 tag before you upgrade a consumer. The notes below are the operator extract. Commit <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/commit/63bf91405cf97b114a84f337fb1272d98a267999" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">63bf914</a> and <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1277" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1277</a> are the contract change.
        </p>
        <h3>Success payload</h3>
        <p>Evidence-producing tools return the complete Evidence record in <code>structuredContent</code> and in the JSON text. The old <code>{`{ result, evidence_id, evidence }`}</code> wrapper is gone.</p>
        <pre><code>{`// 6.1
const value = reply.structuredContent.result;
const evidence = reply.structuredContent.evidence;

// 6.2 and later, including the 6.9.0 pin
const evidence = reply.structuredContent;
const value = evidence.normalized_result;
const evidenceId = evidence.evidence_id;`}</code></pre>
        <p>
          Check <code>isError</code> before success fields. Errors set <code>isError: true</code>, put the typed diagnostic in a text content block, and omit <code>structuredContent</code> so they do not have to match the success schema.
          Lifecycle and other non-Evidence tools keep their own output contracts. Do not assume every successful tool is Evidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every Evidence record requires <code>analysis_profile</code>: the observed profile object, or <code>null</code>. The field is part of Evidence identity.
          Inserting <code>null</code> into an old file does <strong>not</strong> preserve the old <code>evidence_id</code>. Keep the original and regenerate with 6.2 or later. Records that already match the full canonical contract stay usable.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>binary_session</code> no longer has top-level <code>provider</code> and <code>providers</code> aliases. Read <code>analysis_provider_binding</code>, <code>analysis_provider_candidates</code>, and per-operation <code>capabilities</code>.
          Select a deep provider with <code>open_binary.provider_id</code> or CLI <code>--provider</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          A transport <code>resource_constraint</code> can carry <code>details.reported_limits.evidence_reference</code>. Consume the retained Evidence on the same connection with <code>inspect_analysis_view</code> or <code>export_evidence_bundle</code>.
          Response budgets are fixed when the server starts. Recreate the server to change them. Raising the server budget does not raise the client’s receive limit.
        </p>
        <h3>Snapshots and artifact roles</h3>
        <p>Snapshots require <code>workflow_entries</code> and a profile-bound Evidence record for every cached query. Import rejects incomplete bindings. Keep the old snapshot and write a new path, for example:</p>
        <pre><code>npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 analyze /absolute/path/to/program --provider ghidra --snapshot /absolute/path/to/analysis/program-6.4.json</code></pre>
        <p>In MCP, open without the incompatible <code>snapshot_path</code>, run the queries, then save through <code>close_binary.snapshot_path</code>. Do not invent missing provider profiles.</p>
        <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Read before 6.2</th><th>Read in 6.2+</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>nodes[].kind</code></td><td><code>occurrences[].artifact_kind</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Path-specific <code>nodes[].format</code></td><td><code>occurrences[].artifact_format</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>nodes[].executable</code></td><td><code>occurrences[].executable</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Content identity and byte format</td><td><code>nodes[].artifact_id</code>, <code>sha256</code>, <code>format</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Join an occurrence to its content node with <code>artifact_id</code>. Identical bytes can share a node and still have different path roles. A merged content node cannot recover per-path facts that were never stored. Regenerate old inventories.</p>
        <h3>Other 6.2 consumer breaks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Process captures.</strong> Legacy v3 conversion on import is gone (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/commit/2a7746998d47446c4db6d4f524e0f183d6803f3f" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">2a77469</a>). Captures need explicit selected/launch executable identity and <code>event_journal</code>. An empty journal is valid; an omitted journal is not. Keep old captures as history and recapture when you need a current comparison. Do not invent launch identity from a later digest, or event order from separate logs.</li>
          <li><strong>Filesystem effects</strong> may report <code>status: "unknown"</code> with a reason. Unknown is not “absent”.</li>
          <li><strong>Cleanup.</strong> A finished one-shot analysis can report <code>cleanup_incomplete</code> instead of silent success when provider cleanup fails (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1211" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1211</a>). Keep <code>details.partial_observation</code> or the primary diagnostic. A good observation does not prove cleanup.</li>
          <li><strong>JavaScript projections</strong> require <code>presence</code> of <code>present</code>, <code>absent</code>, or <code>unknown-coverage</code>. Unknown values and unknown presence are different. Object operations use <code>properties.property_path</code> (segments or <code>null</code>), not a flattened name.</li>
          <li><strong>Function comparisons</strong> use <code>unchanged</code>, <code>changed</code>, or <code>unknown</code>. The <code>truncated</code> status and <code>summary.truncated</code> counter are gone.</li>
          <li><strong>Symlinks</strong> with <code>target_state</code> <code>unreadable</code> or <code>unknown</code> require <code>target: null</code>. External targets keep the observed absolute path. A display placeholder such as <code>&lt;outside-root&gt;</code> is not lookup data. Reimport those graphs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="captures">6.3.0 — capture producer accounting</h2>
        <p>
          Published 2026-10-09. Historical captures that lack current producer accounting or transaction identity are rejected, and web diffs that omit accessibility or storage dimensions are rejected
          (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/commit/3283a45d09457c79e3adadb50a48620926d4bc5b" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">3283a45</a>).
          Preserve the original capture and recapture with the current producer. Comparison consumers must include every dimension. Do not fill a missing observation so the diff still renders.
        </p>
        <p>Same release, still operator-visible if you store these objects:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>JSON shape paths use typed property and array-element segments. WebMCP <code>input_schema_shape</code> is replaced by <code>input_schema</code> and <code>input_schema_sha256</code>.</li>
          <li>Filesystem digest omissions require <code>system_code</code>. Budget and changed-file omissions use null. Unavailable-file omissions keep the operating-system error code.</li>
          <li>Provider analysis outputs must supply metadata that used to be repaired with defaults. Unsupported nullable facets are <code>null</code>, not omitted.</li>
          <li>JavaScript semantic graphs store evidence context IDs and locations, and results require an inline <code>evidence_contexts</code> table.</li>
          <li>Source-map URLs live on target observations selected by <code>declared_url_sha256</code>. Doctor skill identity no longer emits <code>installed_catalog_digest</code>; use <code>identity.skill.state</code>.</li>
          <li>The never-incremented <code>truncated_scopes</code> statistic is removed from JavaScript application analysis.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="sockets">6.4.0 — WebSocket results and stored graphs</h2>
        <p>Published 2026-10-11. Release: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.4.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.4.0</a>.</p>
        <h3>WebSocket field rename</h3>
        <p>
          Read <code>network.websocket_connections</code>. Do not read <code>network.websocket_events</code>. No legacy alias remains
          (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/commit/db4e3608465486466591b594cf77037ac150c988" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">db4e360</a>).
          Each connection has <code>request_id</code>, <code>url</code>, and <code>events</code>. <code>payload_bytes</code> may be <code>null</code> when the size is unknown. Update dashboards before you call a missing field a capture failure.
        </p>
        <h3>Stored Evidence and graphs</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Saved reference graphs.</strong> Exclusions need their matching <code>pattern</code> and must distinguish <code>project-ignored</code> from <code>default-ignored</code>. Re-import graphs that lack that provenance (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/commit/6585293c562853b95c3a70df02c12ad8cc17afc4" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">6585293</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Artifact graph edges.</strong> Child artifact IDs and paths come from the occurrence selected by <code>occurrence_id</code>, not from edge fields <code>child_artifact_id</code> / <code>logical_path</code>. Older inventory Evidence does not validate against the new commitment (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1493" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1493</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Semantic graph schema.</strong> Nodes and relations no longer include <code>identifier_strategy</code>, and relation IDs no longer hash it. Older Evidence does not validate (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1474" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1474</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Semantic identities.</strong> Select IDs from the parent graph. Read event names from <code>event_name</code>, endpoints from <code>endpoint</code>, and literal values from <code>properties.value</code>. New analyses use digest-based IDs for long or reserved names. Previously stored graphs keep their original IDs and remain valid workflow inputs (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1427" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1427</a> and related).</li>
          <li><strong>Capture comparisons</strong> that use custom normalization must recapture both sides with <code>literal-replacements-v1</code>. Legacy unversioned pattern captures stay readable but cannot be compared with new pattern captures. Captures without patterns are unaffected (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1456" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1456</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Terminal captures</strong> keep the initial and resized buffers within 1,000,000 cells using <code>columns × (rows + scrollback)</code>. Oversized scenarios are rejected before launch.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Library authors, not MCP JSON</h3>
        <p>
          Direct in-process resource APIs now take a caller-owned <code>ArtifactResourceScope</code> (inventory, extraction, JavaScript analysis, reference imports, web exports). For <code>readJavaScriptArtifactFiles</code>, scope is argument three and the abort signal is argument four.
          <strong>CLI and MCP inputs for those operations are unchanged.</strong> If you only call tools over stdio, do not add a scope object to the tool arguments.
        </p>
        <p>Optional agent-verification reports accept schema version 4. Production CLI and MCP contracts for that report are unchanged.</p>


        <h2 id="nulls">6.5.0 — null states, filtered JSON, call graphs, MCP discovery, ADB</h2>
        <p>
          Body date 2026-10-13; GitHub <code>published_at</code> 2026-10-14 12:32 UTC (2026-10-14 20:32 UTC+8).
          Release: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.5.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.5.0</a>.
          Contribution record in the release footer: <strong>893</strong> commits and <strong>529</strong> merged PRs.
          On <strong>2026-10-15</strong> this site’s check recorded npm <code>latest</code> as <strong>6.5.0</strong>. The current check (2026-11-13) is 6.9.0; see the top of this page.
          Rows below are paraphrased from the release <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code> section — do not invent additional breaks.
        </p>
        <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Break</th><th>Operator impact</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Runtime attachment state</td>
                <td><code>attached</code> may be <code>null</code> in JavaScript, browser, and Electron discovery/inspection. Treat null as unknown; do <strong>not</strong> coerce it to false. (e55ef72)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Source maps</td>
                <td>Original-source and mapping rows keep a null source name when unavailable. Handle null; do not invent an unknown-source string. New index fields remain optional when reading older Evidence. (ee50ed1)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Streamed filtered JSON</td>
                <td><code>--filter-output</code> emits JSON <code>null</code> instead of <code>{"{}"}</code> when the selected value is null. Distinguish present null from a missing selection. Use <code>--full-output</code> when an object envelope is required. (#2333)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Call graphs</td>
                <td><code>get_call_graph.normalized_result</code> is now <code>{"{"} graph, limitations {"}"}</code>. Read traversal-depth groups under <code>graph</code> and retain relationship-specific caveats. (5dfb9d0)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>MCP discovery</td>
                <td><code>binary_session</code> no longer repeats <code>server_identity.catalog.tools</code>. Use the connected server tool list, grouped <code>tool_availability</code>, and provider capabilities. (#1988)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Provider admission</td>
                <td>MIPS targets with unresolved GNU ABI attributes are refused — supply supported ABI declarations. Saved Hopper databases on macOS are unavailable (launcher cannot run the analysis bridge when opening a database); select an executable target instead. (d4bd65c)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Segment extents</td>
                <td><code>binary_overview</code> segment length may be null when Hopper cannot establish a finite extent. Preserve unknown; do not coerce to 0 or a saturated value. (36db19c)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Invocation identity</td>
                <td><code>server.command_path</code> may be null; registration/setup statuses or doctor classifications may be unknown. Establish the actual invocation before treating a registration as aligned. (187f113)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>ADB installation</td>
                <td>Optional <code>replace</code> input is unchanged. Results now require <code>replace_requested</code> for the requested <code>adb install -r</code> mode; <code>replaced</code> is nullable because prior device package state was not observed. Do not treat reinstall intent as proof of replacement. (864314a)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Managed/native verification</td>
                <td>Unresolved P/Invoke may retain <code>matched_native</code> and candidates when module identity is unknown. Interpret <code>status</code>, <code>basis</code>, and <code>limitations</code>; unknown module ≠ empty observations. (3f6b575)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          SQLite snapshot inspection in 6.5.0 needs Node <strong>24.x ≥24.15 or 26+</strong> with <code>DatabaseSync.limits</code>. That is a capability gate, not listed under <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code>, but operators on Node 22 / earlier 24 will see the lane refuse.
        </p>
        <p>Also update ADB result readers: see <a href="/docs/android-adb/">Android ADB</a>. Call-graph and MCP discovery consumers should re-check field paths before trusting dashboards built on 6.4.0 shapes.</p>

        <h2 id="kuna">6.6.0 — saved Evidence, browser limits, ADB version codes</h2>
        <p>
          GitHub <code>published_at</code> 2026-10-18 03:40 UTC. Body date 2026-10-18.
          Release: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.6.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.6.0</a>.
          Footer: <strong>571</strong> commits and <strong>236</strong> merged PRs.
          This tag is <strong>not on npm</strong>. <code>npm view rea-agents@6.6.0</code> returned 404 on 2026-11-13, and the 6.7.0 release says the tag was not published.
          The bullets below are the 6.6.0 <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code> section, shortened to the contract.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Saved Evidence.</strong> Evidence and analysis snapshots require explicit nullable <code>relationship_coverage</code>. Artifact inventories require scoped coverage and explicit <code>integrity_contradictions</code>. Obsolete <code>coverage_status</code> and prose-based coverage inference are removed. Regenerate old Evidence, snapshots, and inventory observations. Saved files are not migrated, and omitted facts are not filled with guessed defaults (db8128d, 0405c9d, a9588be).</li>
          <li><strong>Browser capture results.</strong> Retain resolved capture limits, event families, and omission facts. Omitted caller inputs still select defaults, but stored observations must report the resolved values. Admitted content reads queue behind bounded concurrency (57a23f0).</li>
          <li><strong>Android version codes.</strong> <code>inspect_adb_package.version_code</code> is a decimal string, not a JSON number. Read it as a string, or use <code>BigInt</code> for numeric comparison (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/3485" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#3485</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Native UI failures.</strong> Failed or cancelled native UI scenarios return typed errors with the collected report in <code>partial_observation</code>. Do not expect a successful result that contains failed steps (d909919).</li>
          <li><strong>Provider status.</strong> <code>binary_session</code> candidate availability can be unknown during owner finalization. Preserve that state rather than treating it as unavailable (150e996).</li>
          <li><strong>Swift symbol locations.</strong> <code>swift_symbols</code> entries may have a null <code>address</code> when the provider supplies no location. Optional <code>evidence.reported_address</code> retains the original provider value (8116dc0).</li>
          <li><strong>Linux Hopper admission.</strong> Older builds previously admitted by a fixed allowlist need retained publisher-signed package evidence or an approved update to the current public demo. Update explicit <code>HOPPER_LAUNCHER_PATH</code> selections. The official RPM metadata mismatch remains unresolved and is refused (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/3590" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#3590</a>).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="six-seven">6.7.0 — no breaking section of its own</h2>
        <p>
          GitHub <code>published_at</code> 2026-10-18 07:45 UTC. npm time 2026-10-18T08:12:05Z.
          Release: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.7.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.7.0</a>.
          Footer of the 6.7-only note: <strong>4</strong> commits and <strong>1</strong> merged PR.
        </p>
        <p>
          The 6.7.0 heading has <strong>no</strong> <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code> section. Its Changes section says the release includes the 6.6.0 changes and migration notes, and that 6.6.0 was tagged but not published to npm.
          Installing npm <code>6.7.0</code> is therefore the first published package that carries the 6.6 breaks above. Do not invent a separate 6.7 field break.
          The 6.7-only fix, which the release does not label breaking, is that setup edits the last repeated JSON/JSONC member and refuses a removal that would reactivate a shadowed duplicate (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/4957" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#4957</a>).
        </p>

        <h2 id="formats">6.8.0 — Node floor, compact schemas, summaries, JSON Lines</h2>
        <p>
          GitHub <code>published_at</code> 2026-10-25 08:36 UTC. Body date 2026-10-25. npm time 2026-10-25T09:07:31Z.
          Release: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.8.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.8.0</a>.
          Footer: <strong>1740</strong> commits and <strong>497</strong> merged PRs.
          The same Node string is still <code>engines.node</code> in the 6.9.0 package. Rows below are that release’s <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code> bullets.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Function analysis.</strong> <code>analyze_function</code> defaults to a retained summary. Set <code>detail: "complete"</code> for the previous inline dossier. The CLI keeps its complete default and requires <code>--evidence_output</code> when selecting a summary (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5660" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5660</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> Accept JSON numbers and booleans in node <code>value</code>, alongside strings and null (cc90771, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/6759" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#6759</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>JSON Lines.</strong> <code>--format jsonl</code> emits object-collection rows followed by a <code>$rea: "jsonl/v1"</code>, <code>type: "metadata"</code> record. Scalar selections and unsupported reports are refused. Use <code>--format json</code> for the previous whole-document output (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5629" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5629</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Interface Builder.</strong> Keyed-archive graph identities use decimal table UIDs instead of authored <code>objectID</code> / <code>object-id</code>. ibtool and native NIBArchive identities keep their source semantics (6fbe67d).</li>
          <li><strong>Frida.</strong> <code>instrument-with-frida</code> JSON returns the canonical Evidence directly. Read <code>normalized_result.cleanup_error</code> instead of the former top-level wrapper field (48f700e).</li>
          <li><strong>Reconstruction proof.</strong> ID-array proof records no longer establish verified or ready ledgers. Supply implementation/revision bindings and individual claim outcomes (f8b65e7).</li>
          <li><strong>Mach-O imports.</strong> Handle a null import <code>name</code> when identity is ambiguous. Use <code>raw_name</code> and <code>name_status</code> (5d0d243, 169512a).</li>
          <li><strong>Node.js.</strong> Use a runtime satisfying <code>^22.23.4 || ^24.22.1 || &gt;=26.12.1</code>. Node 23 and 25 are unsupported. Upgrade Node before installing or updating REA. The installer does not upgrade it (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/6315" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#6315</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Browser storage.</strong> Historical hashed storage remains readable, but comparisons stay unknown until both captures are recaptured in the new representation (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/6341" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#6341</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Environment serving.</strong> <code>environment-serve</code> serves derived state by default, including write tools whose effects are confirmed by recorded evidence. Use <code>--replay-only</code> for stateless replay. Read stop-summary <code>state</code> instead of <code>state_evidence_id</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5351" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5351</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/6158" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#6158</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>MCP schemas.</strong> Input advertisements default to compact. Set <code>REA_MCP_INPUT_SCHEMA_PROFILE=full</code> for complete advertised guidance and nested constraints (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5975" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5975</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Browser console arguments.</strong> Accept null <code>argument_types</code> and <code>text_capture.status: "unavailable"</code> when the protocol argument inventory is omitted or malformed (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/6016" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#6016</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Reconstruction summaries.</strong> <code>summary.by_evidence_authority</code> is keyed by Evidence authority. Read the former source-state counts from required <code>summary.by_source_state</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5875" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5875</a>).</li>
          <li><strong>Swift bindings.</strong> Conformance <code>type_name</code> and <code>protocol_name</code> may be null. Consume typed <code>type_binding</code> / <code>protocol_binding</code>. The former Objective-C-specific import-binding type is replaced by <code>MachoImportBinding</code> (d0067ba).</li>
          <li><strong>WebSocket frames.</strong> Accept null opcodes and preserve unknown frame facts. Numeric opcodes are restricted to the four-bit protocol range (0bc2b42).</li>
          <li><strong>Resource-only inspection.</strong> Evidence subjects and executable digests may be null. Use <code>resource_root</code> and each resource’s reported provenance (6a6adf7).</li>
          <li><strong>Browser timestamps.</strong> Console and session-timeline timestamps may be null when the protocol supplies no finite/comparable time (690fc51, 2a0410f).</li>
          <li><strong>Reference sources.</strong> Read failed root enumeration from <code>rootFailure</code> rather than a synthetic failed child at <code>"."</code> (6296fdf).</li>
          <li><strong>Filesystem capture.</strong> Accept <code>entry_unavailable</code> and <code>identity_changed</code> enumeration omission reasons in addition to the previous reason literals (c85b44e).</li>
          <li><strong>APK locales.</strong> Replace numeric legacy selectors such as <code>es-r419</code> with <code>es-419</code> or <code>b+es+419</code>. Two-letter regions remain supported (29910d1).</li>
          <li><strong>XML plist scalars.</strong> Recognize <code>$plist_type: "unknown"</code> and read <code>element</code>, <code>literal</code>, and <code>reason</code>. Supported extended UTC years preserve their timestamp (3537e58).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="desktop">6.9.0 — settings, local MCP add, Evidence readers</h2>
        <p>
          Body date 2026-11-11. GitHub <code>published_at</code> 2026-11-12 08:59 UTC (2026-11-12 16:59 UTC+8). npm time 2026-11-12T09:53:32Z.
          Release: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.9.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents-6.9.0</a>.
          Footer: <strong>1848</strong> commits and <strong>1073</strong> merged PRs.
          npm <code>latest</code> on 2026-11-13 17:02:45 CST was 6.9.0.
          Every bullet in that release’s <code>BREAKING CHANGES</code> section is listed below, shortened to the contract. The release body is the full wording. Nothing here is an extra break.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Settings clients replace <code>effect</code>, <code>rea_restart_required</code>, <code>restart_required</code>, and <code>restartRequired</code> with <code>update_mode</code> (<code>runtime</code>, <code>restart</code>, <code>parameter</code>) and <code>pending_restart</code>. Parameter-supplied limits cannot be changed by the runtime setter (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9885" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9885</a>).</li>
          <li>Process and desktop callers inspect <code>details.secondary_failures</code> / <code>secondaryFailures</code>. Mixed batches keep physical/provider failures primary. Retained descriptors can produce <code>cleanup_incomplete</code>. Custom adapters consume owner-issued facts and retain cleanup scopes until release succeeds (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10141" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10141</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10113" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10113</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10109" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10109</a>).</li>
          <li><code>rea mcp add --command</code> accepts a local stdio launcher only. HTTP(S) executable URLs are rejected before settings writes, and package acquisition is removed. Configure remote transports in each client’s native settings (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10102" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10102</a>).</li>
          <li>Runtime-instance graph identities require <code>identity.capture_evidence_id</code> in addition to the capture digest and runtime key. Regenerate reconciliation Evidence (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10063" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10063</a>).</li>
          <li>Retained process symlinks require their stored target bytes. Recapture legacy observations that only described a link (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10082" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10082</a>).</li>
          <li>Function dossiers record Swift literal inventory and its omissions together. Regenerate one-sided observations. Both-absent unsupported observations remain valid (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10068" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10068</a>).</li>
          <li>Conformance manifest schema v2 separates exact string markers from fragments and rejects the old ambiguous <code>strings</code> field. Regenerate unversioned fixtures with <code>npm run build:fixtures</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9977" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9977</a>).</li>
          <li>Unavailable native/BEAM/Go/Rust view collections return <code>items.rows: null</code>, <code>coverage.status: "unavailable"</code>, <code>coverage.total: null</code>, and <code>coverage.exhausted: false</code>. Recorded empty collections still return <code>rows: []</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9893" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9893</a>).</li>
          <li>Desktop witnessing requires the current generated verifier. Re-export old bundles. Pre-6.9 captures missing required <code>state.baseline_non_files</code> are rejected before inspection, drafting, or export (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9898" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9898</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9470" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9470</a>).</li>
          <li>New browser captures record <code>save: []</code> for request actions that save nothing, which changes scenario/Evidence digests. Keep historical digests with historical captures (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9896" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9896</a>).</li>
          <li>Selected SQLite rows require <code>row_offset</code> and <code>next_row_offset</code>. <code>rows.order</code> is <code>rowid</code>, <code>primary_key</code>, or <code>unspecified</code>. A null next offset means either no continuation or no stated order. An unordered sample can still have <code>truncated: true</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9331" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9331</a>).</li>
          <li>Windows entropy Evidence uses the admitted filesystem path spelling, so a differently cased caller path can change <code>evidence_id</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9393" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9393</a>).</li>
          <li><code>caller_input_paths</code> values may be ordered arrays of strings as well as strings (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9626" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9626</a>).</li>
          <li><code>observe_javascript_runtime</code> adds required <code>execution_context_id</code> on scripts and contexts. <code>context_key</code> is an opaque capture-local identity, not a reusable protocol ID (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9471" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9471</a>).</li>
          <li>Refresh cached <code>inspect_address_context</code> schemas: unavailable facets may carry typed input or resource-constraint errors while sibling facets stay available (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8444" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8444</a>).</li>
          <li><code>analyze_function</code> / <code>trace_native_values</code> require <code>native_value_flow.limitations</code> on available and unavailable variants. Ghidra memory effects cover explicit high-p-code <code>LOAD</code>/<code>STORE</code> only. Empty effects do not prove no memory access. The <code>value_flow_effect_scope</code> profile commitment invalidates older snapshots (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8651" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8651</a>).</li>
          <li>Ghidra byte searches require <code>skipped_overlays</code>. Loaded overlays no longer count as not loaded. Reopen targets and save a fresh snapshot after the profile/search-policy changes (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8608" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8608</a>).</li>
          <li><code>compare_functions</code> adds <code>function_match.method: "same-evidence"</code> when both inputs authenticate to one Evidence ID and entry comparison is unavailable. Do not infer complete equivalence (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8442" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8442</a>).</li>
          <li>Kuna <code>analyze_function</code> can return <code>native_value_flow: {"{"} available: false, reason, limitations {"}"}</code> instead of null. Null means procedure-scoped unrecorded unknown, not confirmed absence. Older trace Evidence must be rerun to satisfy current replay (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8785" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8785</a>).</li>
          <li>The opt-in hot/cold MCP catalog no longer preloads <code>inspect_analysis_view</code>. Discover it before use, or batch it with its producer. The default full catalog remains available (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9151" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9151</a>).</li>
          <li><code>batch_decompile</code> and retained batch views use <code>items[].status: "unavailable"</code> with <code>reason: "no_pseudocode"</code> for null pseudocode, replacing the former <code>error</code> / <code>capability_unavailable</code> item. Empty or non-text values remain <code>status: "error"</code> with <code>unreadable_output</code>. Both count toward <code>failed</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8737" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8737</a>).</li>
          <li><code>import_evidence_bundle</code> / CLI <code>evidence-import</code> reject snapshot-shaped JSON with <code>invalid_request</code> instead of <code>evidence_integrity_mismatch</code>. Restore a snapshot with <code>open_binary.snapshot_path</code> or a compatible CLI <code>--snapshot</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8867" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8867</a>).</li>
          <li>REA-launched Chromium keeps its sandbox. If launch fails on root/container hosts, enable host sandbox support first. <code>REA_BROWSER_NO_SANDBOX=true</code> disables Chromium’s sandbox and does not establish an REA isolation boundary (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8738" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8738</a>).</li>
          <li>Fresh objdump Evidence changes provider identity from <code>gnu.objdump</code> / <code>GNU objdump</code> to <code>{"{"} id: "objdump.command", name: "objdump command", version: null {"}"}</code>. Historical Evidence stays readable (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8824" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8824</a>).</li>
          <li>Kuna verification policy is separate from analysis identity. Earlier snapshots and resumable directory exports are incompatible even with the same executable. Preserve old files and save a fresh snapshot or export directory (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8699" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8699</a>). The release points at <code>docs/kuna-provider.md</code> on the repository for extracting embedded Evidence as history.</li>
          <li><code>inspect_analysis_view</code> rejects mismatched native parent predicates with <code>invalid_request</code> at <code>source.predicate_type</code>. Function/inventory/observation views require <code>rea.analysis</code>. Matching views require <code>rea.native-function-matching</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8451" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8451</a>).</li>
          <li><code>trace_feature</code> can succeed when xrefs exist but owner lookup is unavailable. Accept <code>references[].containing_procedure.status: "unavailable"</code>. <code>truncated: false</code> does not establish resolved ownership (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8368" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8368</a>).</li>
          <li><code>close_binary</code> retains investigation records. Use <code>reset_investigation</code> to clear them. Cross-process recovery requires an explicitly acknowledged Evidence-bundle checkpoint (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8361" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8361</a>).</li>
          <li><code>compare_functions</code> also adds matched <code>function_match.method: "same-entry"</code> with required <code>entry_address</code> when artifact, architecture, mapping, slice, and entry commitments agree despite a rename (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8263" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8263</a>).</li>
          <li><code>inspect_native_load_image</code> NativeAOT <code>metadata_recovery</code> uses a status-discriminated union. Complete reports require <code>reason: null</code>. Partial/not-applicable reports carry <code>{"{"} code, ... {"}"}</code> instead of prose reasons. Invalid budgets produce typed input/resource errors (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8053" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8053</a>).</li>
          <li><code>trace_javascript_semantics</code> adds <code>influences</code> edges and moves direct literal-argument seeds from call-site to expression nodes. Relevant unknown dependencies can change <code>found</code> to <code>partial</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7939" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7939</a>).</li>
          <li><code>inspect_managed_members</code> changes <code>signature_resolution</code> from <code>type-names-v1</code> to <code>type-names-v2</code> and appends readable names to signature operands. Signature digests are unchanged. <code>InternalCall</code> methods remain runtime-provided boundaries (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5309" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5309</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9547" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9547</a>).</li>
          <li>MCP calls default to <strong>1,024</strong> combined array elements and object members. Excess input is rejected before dispatch as nonretryable <code>resource_constraint</code>, <code>resource: "transport"</code>. Set <code>REA_MCP_MAX_INPUT_ELEMENTS</code> to a digit-only positive decimal safe integer (1–9007199254740991) and restart, or select retained/file inputs. Inputs are never truncated (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7905" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7905</a>).</li>
          <li><code>inspect_macho</code> text names/paths can be null for non-UTF-8 bytes, with hex companion fields. Unsafe numeric sizes/offsets/alignments can be null with exact companion fields. Delayed-init <code>options</code> are numeric (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7952" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7952</a>).</li>
          <li>Environment file-source errors move from the generic <code>evidence</code> issue path to <code>capture</code> for <code>environment-build</code> and <code>source.path</code> for environment bundle build/export. Missing or invalid sources return <code>invalid_request</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7900" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7900</a>).</li>
          <li>Selected unpaired UTF-16 surrogates make TOON, Markdown, CSV, and TSV output fail with <code>invalid_request</code> even after a successful operation. Markdown also refuses NUL. Use <code>--format json</code> or <code>--format yaml</code> to preserve the values (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7852" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7852</a>).</li>
          <li>Reconstruction <code>evidence_bundle</code> inputs reject authenticated standalone records as <code>invalid_request</code> instead of treating them as damaged bundles. Supply a canonical bundle from <code>export_evidence_bundle</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7895" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7895</a>).</li>
          <li>Environment coverage can use <code>method-replay</code> for non-GET safe reads. Clock-generating write plans without a global clock anchor return <code>served: false</code>, <code>reason: "unknown-clock"</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7834" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7834</a>).</li>
          <li>Ghidra returns <code>not-in-listing</code> for in-memory addresses lacking listed instructions or defined data, replacing the former <code>undecodable</code> interpretation (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7823" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7823</a>).</li>
          <li><code>capture_process_scenario</code> / CLI process capture rejects <code>columns: 1</code> before target launch. Terminal widths must be at least 2. Sensitive interaction <code>data</code> is empty with <code>sensitive</code> / <code>input_bytes</code>, and raw echoes are redacted (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7848" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7848</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7804" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7804</a>).</li>
          <li>Managed setup registrations bind the selected absolute runtime and REA entry script, including package-runner cache paths. Setup no longer returns <code>prewarm</code> or emits its progress events (c77735fa83a6).</li>
          <li>macOS Hopper launch paths and arguments reject double quotes, backslashes, and line breaks before handoff (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7732" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7732</a>).</li>
          <li>New JavaScript application graphs omit the derived package <code>renderer</code> property. Use <code>renderer_declarations</code> and package-load edges. Historical Evidence remains readable (5cf7133f823b).</li>
          <li>Replace Cutter <code>--json=true/false</code> with <code>--json-output=true/false</code>. Bare <code>--json</code> still selects CLI result formatting. Replace <code>rea compare-bundles</code> with <code>rea compare</code>. MCP <code>compare_bundles</code> is unchanged (567ea4b1e8bb, 3515b262218f).</li>
          <li>JEB engine refusals report <code>execution_failure</code> rather than <code>unsupported_target</code> (c4cdb7658b0e).</li>
          <li>ASAR file occurrences may contain <code>unpacked: false</code>. Absent historical fields remain unknown (60834e391c3f).</li>
          <li>Non-loopback MCP HTTP binds require <code>MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS</code> or <code>rea mcp --http --allowed-hosts</code>. Bundle names must be unchanged HTTP hostnames within the 63-octet DNS-label limit (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7172" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7172</a>).</li>
          <li><code>binary_session {"{}"}</code> is compact by default and omits provider availability, target-support diagnostics, and tool-group surface. Request <code>{"{"} "detail": "complete" {"}"}</code> for those facts (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7127" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7127</a>).</li>
          <li>Native input errors include <code>details.operation</code> and field-level <code>details.issues</code>. <code>trace_native_values.procedure</code> must be nonempty (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7889" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7889</a>).</li>
          <li>Readable JavaScript members that normalize to one logical path stop <code>analyze_javascript_application</code> with <code>artifact_operation_failed</code>, <code>details.reason: "path"</code>, and a partial inventory (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7864" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7864</a>).</li>
          <li><code>trace_web_module_imports</code> with an empty or relative <code>REA_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE</code> reports <code>capability_unavailable</code> with <code>invalid_browser_executable</code> instead of <code>missing_browser_executable</code>. An unset selection still means missing (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7903" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7903</a>).</li>
          <li>Unresolvable <code>import-reference-source</code> roots, capture scenario files, and web-network capture/Protobuf descriptor paths (<code>ELOOP</code> / <code>ENAMETOOLONG</code>) report <code>invalid_request</code> / <code>invalid_input</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7847" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7847</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7814" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7814</a>).</li>
          <li><code>close_binary</code> with <code>snapshot_path</code> on a profileless/archive target returns nonretryable <code>capability_unavailable</code> instead of <code>evidence_integrity_mismatch</code>, writes no snapshot, and leaves the session open (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7837" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7837</a>).</li>
          <li>adb local-file refusals occur before device commands. Missing or non-file <code>local_path</code> / <code>apk_path</code>, and a file-blocked <code>output_directory</code>, return <code>invalid_request</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7885" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7885</a>).</li>
          <li>Evidence writes failing with <code>EFBIG</code>, <code>ENOSPC</code>, or <code>EDQUOT</code> report nonretryable <code>resource_constraint</code>, <code>details.reason: "storage-limit"</code>. A failed staged-file cleanup remains <code>cleanup_incomplete</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7887" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7887</a>).</li>
          <li>PE signers add optional nullable <code>unsigned_attribute_oids</code>. Fresh null means absent. An OID array means present. Omission in old Evidence is unrecorded. Unsigned attributes produce <code>coverage.status: "partial"</code> (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/7920" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#7920</a>).</li>
          <li>Valid ASN.1 exceeding certificate nesting or OID allowances returns nonretryable <code>resource_constraint</code> rather than <code>invalid_request</code>, with <code>max_asn1_depth</code> / <code>max_oid_bytes</code>. Those bounds have no runtime override (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9932" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9932</a>).</li>
          <li><code>trace_call_path</code> / <code>build_call_path</code> require discovery and observed-result fields in <code>search_scope</code>. An exhausted observed graph can still yield <code>goal_status: "unknown"</code> when provider discovery is incomplete (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8443" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8443</a>).</li>
          <li><code>inspect_native_instruction</code> adds <code>containing_instruction</code> for <code>not-instruction-boundary</code> and <code>containing_data</code> for <code>data</code>. The Ghidra profile changes: reopen and save a fresh snapshot (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8777" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8777</a>).</li>
          <li><code>trace_native_values</code> adds required <code>page_truncated</code> and tagged <code>traversal</code> coverage. <code>truncated</code> combines page omission with traversal truncation. Exactly filling a budget alone no longer proves truncation (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8309" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8309</a>).</li>
          <li><code>batch_decompile.addresses</code> has a separate hard ceiling of <strong>20,000</strong> entries. Raising the MCP transport allowance cannot remove it (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5937" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5937</a>).</li>
          <li><code>close_binary</code> can retire the target while retaining cleanup owners. <code>cleanup_incomplete</code> may have <code>recovery.kind: "retry_cleanup"</code> despite <code>retryable: false</code>. Call <code>close_binary</code> again without <code>snapshot_path</code> on the same connection (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8329" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8329</a>).</li>
          <li>Unconfirmed cleanup in <code>inspect_address_context</code>, <code>get_call_graph</code>, or <code>trace_call_path</code> produces tool-level <code>cleanup_incomplete</code> rather than a successful partial result (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8417" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8417</a>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/8516" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#8516</a>).</li>
          <li><code>inspect_ntfs_journal</code> omits detailed <code>mftMetadata.record_headers</code> by default and leaves continuation at the first omitted record. Select <code>mft_record_limit</code> from 1 to 32 when those details are needed (1a8a9b749a).</li>
          <li>Desktop state directories use <code>application.state_directories[].exists_at_start: null</code> plus <code>existence_error</code> when inspection fails. Accept the tri-state field (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/9899" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#9899</a>).</li>
        </ul>

